# Registries

- New sandbox backends register via `registry.Register` in `main`, not scattered `switch provider` on string names.
- Provider `Name()` returns a stable lowercase identifier (`sprites`, `modal`, `e2b`, `docker`, `daytona`, `blaxel`).
- Lookup uses `registry.Get(name)`; unknown names return a clear error at config validation time when possible.
- Do not hardcode provider lists in help text; derive from `registry.Names()` when listing supported providers.
- A provider with an official Go SDK uses that SDK (Sprites, Modal, Daytona, Blaxel); one without an official Go SDK uses an internal client in its package (E2B, Docker). Hide either behind small interfaces so tests run on fakes.
